WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.665
Before beginning the next task, pause in a safe position.

2
00:00:06.365 --> 00:00:08.485
Let your hands rest for a moment.

3
00:00:10.185 --> 00:00:15.130
Notice the surface beneath you and one sound nearby.

4
00:00:22.335 --> 00:00:24.495
Something came before this pause.

5
00:00:26.195 --> 00:00:32.030
It may feel finished, unfinished, satisfying, or difficult.

6
00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:37.200
You do not need to review it now.

7
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:50.220
On the next exhale, imagine setting it beside you rather than carrying it into every part of what comes next.

8
00:00:59.226 --> 00:01:02.186
Feel one ordinary breath arrive and leave.

9
00:01:03.886 --> 00:01:08.286
Do not make it deeper for the sake of focus.

10
00:01:09.986 --> 00:01:14.366
Let the breath show that this moment has already begun.

11
00:01:23.372 --> 00:01:26.132
Notice where attention is being pulled.

12
00:01:27.832 --> 00:01:36.682
There may be several tabs, messages, worries, or ideas asking to go first.

13
00:01:38.382 --> 00:01:46.477
Name them quietly as many things, without deciding that any of them is wrong.

14
00:01:57.284 --> 00:01:59.844
Now choose one next point of attention.

15
00:02:01.544 --> 00:02:03.504
Not the whole project.

16
00:02:05.204 --> 00:02:07.204
Not the perfect outcome.

17
00:02:08.904 --> 00:02:20.969
Choose the first visible action: open the document, read the question, place the materials, write one sentence, or make one call.

18
00:02:31.776 --> 00:02:35.336
Say that action silently in simple words.

19
00:02:37.036 --> 00:02:45.051
If it is still too large, make it smaller until it can be started without a debate.

20
00:02:54.057 --> 00:02:58.732
Feel the body that will do this action.

21
00:03:00.432 --> 00:03:05.687
Notice feet or seat, hands, and the direction of the gaze.

22
00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:11.772
Let the posture become alert enough, not rigid.

23
00:03:13.472 --> 00:03:16.192
Keep whatever support makes the task sustainable.

24
00:03:26.999 --> 00:03:34.019
For three natural breaths, let the chosen action be the only item you rehearse.

25
00:03:35.719 --> 00:03:41.809
When another thought appears, acknowledge it and return to this one beginning.

26
00:03:56.819 --> 00:04:07.594
Check whether anything essential is missing: water, a tool, a boundary, or a brief message that prevents confusion.

27
00:04:09.294 --> 00:04:14.449
Add only what is genuinely needed to start.

28
00:04:23.455 --> 00:04:27.600
Look at the place where the first action will happen.

29
00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:36.760
This practice does not guarantee concentration, and wandering later is not failure.

30
00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.260
It gives you a clear return point.

31
00:04:47.465 --> 00:04:49.065
Take one final breath.

32
00:04:50.765 --> 00:04:56.260
As it leaves, move directly into the small action you named.

33
00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.000
Begin there.
